Sahara 0001: build Fenix against Mozilla's published GeckoView instead of compiling Gecko.

The root build always includes ':geckoview' as a source project, which needs Java generated by a
full Gecko build. Without it, android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/build.gradle
(getGeckoViewDependency) resolves org.mozilla.geckoview:geckoview-omni-arm64-v8a:<version> from
maven.mozilla.org, where <version> is 157.0.<MOZ_BUILD_DATE>. The tree already supports this case
(see the findProject(":geckoview") checks in android-components/build.gradle and engine-gecko).

Hooks: settings.gradle, the include/projectDir lines for ':geckoview'.

--- a/settings.gradle	2026-10-09 20:31:31.580678669 +0000
+++ b/settings.gradle	2026-10-09 20:31:31.592305323 +0000
@@ -45,11 +45,11 @@
 System.setProperty('android.home', gradle.mozconfig.substs.ANDROID_SDK_ROOT)
 
 include ':annotations', ':messaging_example', ':port_messaging_example'
-include ':geckoview'
+// Sahara: GeckoView is not built from this tree. Android Components then resolves Mozilla's published
+// release build (org.mozilla.geckoview:geckoview-omni-<abi>) instead; see build-config/mozconfig.
 include ':android-components'
 
 project(':annotations').projectDir = new File("${gradle.mozconfig.topsrcdir}/mobile/android/annotations")
-project(':geckoview').projectDir = new File("${gradle.mozconfig.topsrcdir}/mobile/android/geckoview")
 project(':android-components').projectDir = new File("${gradle.mozconfig.topsrcdir}/mobile/android/android-components")
 
 if (!gradle.mozconfig.substs.MOZ_ANDROID_SUBPROJECT || gradle.mozconfig.substs.MOZ_ANDROID_SUBPROJECT == "fenix") {
